meta {
  name: 06-UploadPhoto
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/api/listings/{{amakaListingId}}/photos
  body: multipartForm
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{amakaJwt}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  file: @file(/Users/lukasio/DreamDevs/DreamHomes/haven/audit/assets/amaka/lekki-flat-living-room.jpg) @contentType(image/jpeg)
  caption: Living room — north-facing balcony view
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.id: isDefined
  res.body.url: isDefined
  res.body.displayOrder: isNumber
}

script:post-response {
  bru.setVar("amakaPhotoId", res.body.id);
}

docs {
  # Funke arrived with my phone. We're uploading the living-room photo
  # first.

  ✅ Upload worked. I got back a photo ID, a URL, and a displayOrder.

  ⚠️ I can only upload ONE FILE PER REQUEST. To put 6 photos up I have to
  hit this endpoint 6 times. On a slow Abuja connection, a bulk-upload
  endpoint would save me a lot of time and data. Funke says "is this
  buffering?" three times.

  ⚠️ I had to upload my own picture and trust the platform with the storage.
  No information back about file size limits, or what gets done with the
  image (resized? watermarked? CDN'd?). Spec only says "image/jpeg, png,
  webp" but doesn't tell me how big a file I can send.
}
